      <title>China-linked battery projects could receive UK funding despite security warnings</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/25/china-battery-projects-uk-funding-security-warnings</link>
      <description>China-made lithium-ion batteries, which are relatively low-cost, dominate Ofgem project shortlist A string of battery projects linked to China are expected to be granted UK state subsidies despite deepening fears over the risk of foreign interference they could pose to Europe’s energy systems. Ofgem, Great Britain’s energy regulator, published a provisional shortlist for a new “long duration” energy storage scheme in June. The list was dominated by projects relying on lithium-ion batteries…</description>
